      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2014 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND",
            "content": "Coronary atherosclerotic unstable plaque is one of the leading causes of cardiovascular death. Macrophage-derived matrix metalloproteinase (MMP) 9 is considered for degrading extracellular matrix and collagen, thereby thinning the fibrous cap in plaques. miR-21 is implicated to play an important role in the progression of atherosclerosis. Nevertheless, miR-21 as the biomarker for coronary atherosclerotic unstable plaque remains unknown. We aimed to investigate the prediction role of miR-21 for unstable plaque by pathway study of miR-21 on MMPs and its inhibitor RECK in macrophages."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "Expression of miR-21 in macrophages and serum miR-21 as well as MMP-9 was measured in patients with coronary non-calcified plaque, calcified plaque and controls. In vitro experiment was done in human macrophages by over-expressing miR-21 or down-regulating RECK. The regulation of RECK and MMP-9 by miR-21 was evaluated by western blotting and siRNA strategy."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "Patients with non-calcified coronary artery lesions had significantly higher miR-21 in macrophages and lower miR-21 serum levels compared to the control and calcified plaque patients. At the same time, the serum levels of MMP-9 were significantly elevated in non-calcified patients. Experiments in vitro indicated that over-expressing miR-21 could induce the expression and secretion of pro-MMP-9 and active-MMP-9 in human macrophages via targeting gene RECK, and knocking down RECK expression by specific siRNA can resemble that of miR-21 over-expression."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "miR-21 might be a biomarker for plaque instability by suppressing target gene RECK to promote the expression and secretion of MMP-9 in macrophages."
          }
        ]
      },
